1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,290
You're crossing a
street downtown

2
00:00:01,290 --> 00:00:03,860
when the horizon
starts to climb.

3
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:05,130
One peak
is rising

4
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:07,090
to one hundred
kilometres.

5
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:09,030
Eleven Everests,
stacked.

6
00:00:09,030 --> 00:00:11,200
Clouds barely
reach its ankles.

7
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:12,250
Climb it.

8
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,910
At nine kilometres
you pass Everest,

9
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:16,700
breathing a third
of the oxygen.

10
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:18,090
At nineteen,

11
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:20,450
water boils at
body temperature,

12
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:22,650
even the saliva
on your tongue.

13
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:25,170
By thirty, the noon
sky turns black.

14
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:26,110
At eighty,

15
00:00:26,110 --> 00:00:28,150
meteors burn
up beside you.

16
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:29,910
The summit
is in space.

17
00:00:29,910 --> 00:00:30,910
Over ninety
percent

18
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:32,900
of its height is
a death zone.

19
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:35,010
It's also a
wall nine times

20
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:36,470
taller than
the weather.

21
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,270
One side drowns;

22
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:40,000
the other turns
to desert.

23
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:41,970
But Earth
can't hold it.

24
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:43,370
Its base feels
twenty-six

25
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:45,030
thousand atmospheres.

26
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:47,550
Granite crushes
long before that.

27
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:48,650
The rock flows,

28
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:49,550
the peak sinks,

29
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:51,810
and the horizon
goes flat again.

30
00:00:51,810 --> 00:00:53,200
Where would you
be standing?
